port 21 (FTP), port 80 (HTTP), port 443 (HTTPS) and so on.

To make an ssh connection, you'll need to connect from the client (Your PC or device) to the server which can either be an IP address or a domain name through 2 methods:

i. Password authentication which is not really advicable because it's not really secure due to the fact that the attacker might have run deep reconnaisance on you to have gottten your 
password to access it.

ii. ssh-key authentication: This is considered the most secured because it uses an assymetric form of cryptography for authentication. 
